<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carl Zeiss AG</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1846</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Zeiss</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Carl Zeiss AG is a German optics company that began as a workshop opened in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jena">Jena</a> in 1846 by Carl Zeiss. With the physicist Ernst Abbe and the glassmaker Otto Schott it became a world leader in microscopes, lenses and precision optics. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> it was split into East and West German companies, reunited after 1990 with headquarters in Oberkochen.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carl-zeiss-ag.jpg" alt="Carl Zeiss AG" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carl Zeiss · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zeiss_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
